Scribblenauts unlimited is a fun little game (mostly a game for kids though) about traveling the world and collecting stars by doing lots of "chores" and getting payed with shards and stars which in the end help with freeing your sibling from a petrifying curse. you have a notebook which makes everything you write on it become a real object. you can costumize and create almost anything
Cons:
- since a "chore" has at least 10 ways to clear it, doing them is a bit tooooooo easy, nothing challenging in my opinion;
- its graphisc might not appeal to some;
- little to no replayability;
- if played alot in a short time (a day) can get boring pretty fast;
Pros:
- fun and short game;
- easy to 100%;
- while not challenging it still helps improve imagination, writting speed ( did to me:)) );
- despite doing stuff at a really fast speed there are quite a large number of "chores"to do and explore the fun world;
- fun to play around with random objects and properties;

