Pretty enjoyable game, if you are into strategy give this game a try. You'll die a lot untill you learn the best strategies and how to play with each class.
Pros:
- Beautiful graphics;
- Good music;
- Diversity of weapons, classes, monsters, maps and items;
- It is fun.
Cons:

- The price isn't friendly, I recommend this game if it's in on sale (Idk why steam has so many overpriced games);
- It is not a long game, you could beat it really fast without getting most achievements;
- Some achievements are really hard to get. (beating everything in the hardest difficulty is pretty hard, not a pro for me).

Bought for nostalgia, played for fun. Fallout 3 gives in 3D many of the emotions the previous chapter delivered in 2D.
Pros:
+ a well round world, where someone has faith in mankind and someone else kills for his life;
+ player class is relatively free - but I fear some skills like "Speech" and "Lockpick" will never be ignored;
+ the atmosphere is well built: nostalgic music, misconceptions and ignorance;
Cons:
- a VERY BAD POINT for stability: the game crashed so often to make me nervous. I edited the INI file to limit to 2 the threads and it fixed up most of the issues, but sometimes I still experience crashes (most notably when drinking in 1st person camera view). Bad, bad, bad bug that generate frustration;
- quest pointers and Washington DC navigability are sometimes horrible. Better to focus on common sense;
- bobbleheads locations are so well hidden to make it impossible to find them without googling.
A must for the nostalgics, for the Bethesda lovers and the Nuclear Apocalypse enthusiasts.

